select 've-front-of-house', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD 2, 2026-10-31 (Logan). Visit bounties, the monthly check-in and report, and the monthly rotation (in progress). Full detail: CLAUDE.md in lesaruss/vegansexplore-com, section "BrandDesk". Branch claude/gifted-cori-ummpqg.

1. VISIT BOUNTIES. LIVE on vegansexplore.com (merged). A weekly visit to a managed restaurant is a claim gig (ve_bounties.gig_kind 'visit', visit_listing_id), posted from Depot > BrandDesk > a client > Member visits (ve-bounties visit_get / visit_post / visit_cancel). Defaults: 150 points, 3 a week, at least 3 photos, claims 6 days plus 2 to upload, optional perk, repeat weekly (the hourly ve-bounties cron posts next week's while the client is active). Members tap I'm here (phone within 150 m of the pin plus up to 100 m accuracy; a fix worse than 500 m refused), upload photos, answer "Was your meal on the house?" (FTC). Approval pays the points and copies the photos into the client's Library. Migration 20261031_visit_bounties.sql. Proven live on a [TEST] client, then removed. Not yet: crediting the best photos on the listing and socials; the scouting list.

2. THE MONTHLY CHECK-IN AND REPORT. LIVE (merged). ve_branddesk_checkins, one per client a month. Cron ve-branddesk-checkins (13:07 UTC) opens this month's for every active client that joined before the month, assigned to the chapter's Community Manager (else the team inbox), reminder from the 10th. /business/checkin: How the month went, What's coming, Next month (campaign from the rotation), then The report (what the month meant, what we do next, beside the owner's view). Sending freezes the month's numbers (ve_branddesk_month_numbers: page views, people, actions, check-ins, visits, Library files, against the month before), emails the owner, and the report opens on their dashboard under Managed by us > Monthly reports. Migration 20261031_branddesk_checkins.sql. Proven live on a [TEST] client, then removed. Not yet: Google and social numbers in the report; a Community Manager's view of all their accounts.

3. THE MONTHLY ROTATION. IN PROGRESS, on the branch only, NOT deployed or merged. Done: table ve_branddesk_campaigns (migration 20261031_branddesk_rotation.sql, APPLIED to the database); ve-branddesk code (CAMPAIGNS idea library with a blueprint per kind: influencer night, DJ night, customer appreciation, giveaway, scavenger hunt stop, community night with a coaching sheet, photo night every two months; actions campaign_library, campaign_list, campaign_get, campaign_create, campaign_save, campaign_calendar which puts it on the Vegans Explore calendar hosted by the restaurant; checkin_send now plans next month's campaign and a due photo night; client() returns campaigns) compiled but NOT deployed; page /business/campaign (business/campaign.html: The plan, The blueprint, How it went; ?preview=1 sample); Your campaigns on the client's dashboard (ve-branddesk-client.js view 'campaigns', with Add a campaign for super admins; sample data). Still to do: deploy ve-branddesk from the branch commit through ve-function-deploy and check the source hash; Depot > BrandDesk rotation board (#rotation: every client's campaigns by month); Preview journeys > BrandDesk steps for the campaign page and Your campaigns; browser checks at desktop and phone; prove live on a [TEST] client (send a check-in with a campaign, see next month's planned, set a date, tick the blueprint, put it on the calendar, record results, mark done, owner sees it), then remove the test rows and the test event; document in CLAUDE.md; merge only when Sean says.

Then in the build order: the social add-on and the ad console. Open items for Sean: the first real pitches (warm list, openings, sending), and the BrandDesk trademark and domain check.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
